1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:04,632
Meet Cheddar Hub, my customizable
Raspberry Pi home dashboard.

2
00:00:04,848 --> 00:00:08,518
I began by creating Cheddar,
an animated mascot that gives

3
00:00:08,518 --> 00:00:10,351
the interface its personality.

4
00:00:11,007 --> 00:00:14,693
With AI-assisted coding, I
built and refined a Flask

5
00:00:14,711 --> 00:00:16,432
dashboard running on the Pi.

6
00:00:18,024 --> 00:00:22,272
The live screen combines time,
system health, and everyday tools.

7
00:00:22,599 --> 00:00:26,303
Flask serves it, while Chromium
runs the touchscreen kiosk.

8
00:00:27,043 --> 00:00:30,675
Touch-friendly navigation makes
it easy to move between Home,

9
00:00:30,828 --> 00:00:33,293
Media, and other dashboard pages.

10
00:00:35,007 --> 00:00:37,458
YouTube and YouTube Music
are built in.

11
00:00:37,929 --> 00:00:43,447
Getting audio working through the
WM8960 soundboard took trial and error.

12
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:47,795
I tested the working prototype
repeatedly, fixing touchscreen

13
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:51,789
glitches and troubleshooting graphics
freezes to improve reliability.

14
00:00:52,048 --> 00:00:56,083
In Fusion 360, I designed the
enclosure around the display,

15
00:00:56,164 --> 00:00:58,474
speakers, cables, and cooling.

16
00:00:59,003 --> 00:01:02,462
Later development added
printer telemetry and a tested,

17
00:01:02,525 --> 00:01:04,729
authenticated voice command bridge.

18
00:01:04,956 --> 00:01:08,875
Cheddar Hub: built, tested,
and still evolving.
